{% comment %}
  WILD ROOTS HEMP - THE SCIENCE PAGE TEMPLATE
  ============================================
  This template renders the Science page with:
  - Video hero banner
  - What Is Nano-Hemp definition section
  - 4-step process cards (Raw Hemp → Fragmentation → Encapsulation → Suspension)
  - Comparison table (traditional vs nano-hemp)
  - Four Ingredients section
  - Third-party testing section
  - FAQ accordion
{% endcomment %}

<!-- ==================== HERO BANNER ==================== -->
<section class="hero" aria-label="The Science of Nano-Hemp Hero">
  <video class="hero-video" autoplay muted playsinline preload="auto" aria-hidden="true"
    {% if section.settings.hero_video %}
      poster="{{ section.settings.hero_video | img_url: 'master' }}"
    {% endif %}>
    {% if section.settings.hero_video_url != blank %}
      <source src="{{ section.settings.hero_video_url }}" type="video/mp4">
    {% else %}
      <source src="{{ 'hero-science-lab.mp4' | asset_url }}" type="video/mp4">
    {% endif %}
  </video>
  <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
  <div class="hero-content">
    <span class="hero-label">Proprietary Technology</span>
    <h1 class="hero-title">The Science of Nano-Hemp</h1>
    <p class="hero-subtitle">Why smaller particles make a bigger difference.</p>
  </div>
  <a href="#what-is-nano-hemp" class="hero-scroll" aria-label="Scroll to content">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7" /></svg>
  </a>
</section>

<!-- ==================== MAIN ARTICLE CONTENT ==================== -->
<main itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Article">

  <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: WHAT IS NANO-HEMP? ==================== -->
  <section id="what-is-nano-hemp" class="intro-section section-padding" aria-labelledby="nano-hemp-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="intro-layout">
        <div class="intro-content fade-in" itemprop="articleBody">
          <span class="section-label">Understanding the Technology</span>
          <h2 id="nano-hemp-heading" class="section-title">What Is Nano-Hemp?</h2>
          <p><strong>Nano-hemp is hemp that has been processed using proprietary nano fragmentation technology</strong>, an advanced method that breaks hemp particles down to under 100 nanometers. This dramatic size reduction enables 3-8x better absorption than traditional hemp, allowing nano-particles to pass efficiently through biological membranes for faster, more effective wellness support.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="intro-image fade-in">
          <img src="{{ 'science-intro-illustration.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Elegant botanical illustration showing hemp leaves with nano-particles flowing from large to nano-size" loading="lazy" style="width: 100%; display: block;">
          <div class="intro-image-caption">Proprietary nano fragmentation reduces hemp particles to under 100nm</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="intro-content fade-in" style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">
        <p>The process breaks down hemp particles to <strong>under 100 nanometers</strong> in size. To put that into perspective, a single human hair is approximately 80,000 nanometers wide. That means our nano-hemp particles are roughly 800 times smaller than the width of a human hair, small enough to pass through biological membranes with remarkable efficiency.</p>
        <p>These nano-sized particles are small enough to be absorbed directly through the mucous membranes in your mouth and digestive tract, bypassing many of the barriers that limit traditional hemp absorption. This means dramatically better absorption, faster onset of effects, and more consistent results with every use.</p>

        <!-- Bioavailability Visual -->
        <div class="science-visual fade-in" style="margin: 2.5rem 0; max-width: 900px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(156,175,136,0.15);">
          <img src="{{ 'science-skin-barrier-v2.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Traditional hemp particles (~2,000nm) blocked by skin barrier vs nano-hemp particles (&lt;100nm) passing through" loading="lazy" style="width: 100%; display: block;">
        </div>

        <p>Traditional hemp products contain particles measuring between <strong>5,000 and 10,000 nanometers</strong>, far too large for efficient absorption by the human body. Because the body struggles to process these oversized particles, much of the active compounds pass through without being utilized. Our proprietary nano fragmentation technology, developed by <strong>Ivy League PhD scientists</strong>, solves this problem by reducing particle size by 50-100x.</p>

        <p>The result? <strong>3-8x better bioavailability</strong> compared to traditional hemp products. More of what you take actually reaches your system, which means you need less to achieve the desired effect. It's not just more efficient, it's smarter.</p>

        <div class="intro-highlight">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9.813 15.904L9 18.75l-.813-2.846a4.5 4.5 0 00-3.09-3.09L2.25 12l2.846-.813a4.5 4.5 0 003.09-3.09L9 5.25l.813 2.846a4.5 4.5 0 003.09 3.09L15.75 12l-2.846.813a4.5 4.5 0 00-3.09 3.09z" /></svg>
          50-100x smaller particles than traditional hemp
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Stats Bar -->
      <div class="stats-bar fade-in">
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-number">&lt;100nm</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Particle Size</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-number">3-8x</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Better Absorption</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-item">
          <div class="stat-number">4</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Clean Ingredients</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: PROCESS STAGES ==================== -->
  <section id="three-stages" class="stages-section section-padding" aria-labelledby="stages-heading">
    <div class="root-deco" style="bottom:-50px;left:-80px;"><img src="{{ 'root-illustration.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <span class="section-label">The Process</span>
        <h2 id="stages-heading" class="section-title">From Plant to Nano-Particle</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">Four precise stages transform premium hemp into stable, encapsulated nano-hemp with maximum bioavailability.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stages-grid">
        <!-- Stage 1 -->
        <article class="stage-card fade-in">
          <div class="stage-number">1</div>
          <h3 class="stage-title">Raw Hemp</h3>
          <p class="stage-desc">We start with premium hemp, carefully selected for quality, purity, and potency. Every batch is traced from source to finished product.</p>
        </article>
        <!-- Stage 2 -->
        <article class="stage-card fade-in">
          <div class="stage-number">2</div>
          <h3 class="stage-title">Proprietary Nano Fragmentation</h3>
          <p class="stage-desc">Our breakthrough technology gently breaks down hemp particles to nano-size using a proprietary process developed by Ivy League PhD scientists.</p>
        </article>
        <!-- Stage 3 -->
        <article class="stage-card fade-in">
          <div class="stage-number">3</div>
          <h3 class="stage-title">Nano-Encapsulation</h3>
          <p class="stage-desc">Each nano-particle is individually coated with a protective layer using our clean carrier base. This encapsulation prevents particles from reassembling into large clusters, locking them at nano-size for maximum stability and absorption.</p>
        </article>
        <!-- Stage 4 -->
        <article class="stage-card fade-in">
          <div class="stage-number">4</div>
          <h3 class="stage-title">Stable Suspension</h3>
          <p class="stage-desc">The result is a uniform, water-compatible suspension of individually encapsulated nano-particles that remain stable over time. No shaking, no separation, just consistent potency in every drop.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <!-- Process Visuals -->
      <div style="margin-top: 3rem; max-width: 900px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        <div class="science-visual fade-in" style="border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(156,175,136,0.15); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <img src="{{ 'nano-fragmentation-encapsulation-process.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Four-step process: large hemp clusters are fragmented into nano-particles, then individually encapsulated to prevent reassembly, resulting in stable nano-particles" loading="lazy" style="width: 100%; display: block;">
        </div>
        <div class="science-visual fade-in" style="border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.12); border: 1px solid rgba(156,175,136,0.15); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
          <img src="{{ 'nano-encapsulation-warm.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="Without encapsulation, nano-particles reassemble into large clusters. With encapsulation, each particle stays coated and stable at nano-size." loading="lazy" style="width: 100%; display: block;">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

